WHY (all verified in SDK-COMPOSITION-RESULT.md):
- prospero-clang default target is x86_64-sie-ps5, which rejects
  __attribute__((ms_abi)) at owned_runtime.c:77 (combined_close_handle,
  MFR-3 mutex integration). x86_64-unknown-freebsd9 (the existing bflags
  target used for every abi_c TU) accepts ms_abi; the real owned_runtime.c
  probe-compiles clean under exact bflags (exit 0, zero stderr, 41560-byte
  object) against the failed run's generated headers.
- Target layout equality is already a build-enforced invariant:
  build.py:202-206 compares native-layout (default target) vs bridge-layout
  (bflags) datalayout/values and passed in 1a6b37b7.
- bflags == nflags + '--target=x86_64-unknown-freebsd9' + '-fshort-wchar';
  the probe also passes without -fshort-wchar, so that flag is not
  load-bearing for this TU.

ALTERNATIVES REJECTED:
- Removing ms_abi is not viable: combined_close_handle must call the fixture's
  ms_abi (Win64) CloseHandle pointer; Win64 passes the first argument in RCX vs
  SysV RDI, so a real ms_abi call site is required.
- Moving the thunk into call_workers.c (abi_c, bflags-compiled) works but adds
  a cross-TU symbol and larger source churn for the same effect.

